<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav January trade gap $191 mln.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav January trade gap $191 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	JAN 97     DEC 96	JAN 96</p>
<p> Exports million USD   132	  168	    93</p>
<p> Imports		   323	  396	   231</p>
<p> Balance		  -191	 -169	  -198</p>
<p>NOTES -- January '97 exports rose 42.7 percent on January '96 and imports were 39.7 percent up against the same month last year. Data cover the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, which comprises Serbia and Montenegro. -- Beti Bilandzic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
